  "recorded_utc": "2026-10-29T20:36:35.084493+00:00",
  "scope": "Phase-three Data Resources and default workspace configuration. SDK and viewport rendering/transfer code are unchanged.",
  "status": "Phase three complete; completed_phase is 3. Complex editors, properties, interactions and persistent customization remain in later stages.",
  "implemented": [
    "DataResourceCommands owns shared library catalogs, file and description inputs, native path registration and completion results. Versioned folder/file queries provide copied UTF-8 data. Drawing is SDK-free and does not read files.",
    "Each resource.data instance owns folder, selection, anchor and expansion. Multiple views are independent; the final close collects its catalog and updates remembered paths. Failed navigation, directory refresh and provider replacement preserve existing state.",
    "Resource open/create/refresh/browse/description actions are registered commands. File inputs and description fields reuse the existing native file picker and shared form. DSC writes use existing OutputFiles atomic replacement and retain the original serialization.",
    "Resource input ownership survives view replacement, rejects stale responses, cancels on origin closure and defers accepted answers during native work. Existing file admission prevents overlapping resource and composition forms; completion failures report their destination.",
    "Resource loading queries the primary Level view selection, retaining Script and non-rendering targets. It continues through the existing resource.load/import implementation.",
    "ImGui owns bounded, length-prefixed resource drag bytes with the source row and all files. Schematic, Level, Layout and bitmap Setup use one decoder. Removed fixed 1024-byte paths, EditorState drag copies and resource.dragged.",
    "DefaultWorkspaceConfiguration holds provider choices, seed views, roles, splits, regions, anchors and reset rules. EditorWorkspace owns preparation, immediate runtime layout application, first-use checks and reset. Failed preparation preserves views and configuration. Active operations and modals refuse full layout replacement.",
    "Default seed order retains primary window identities. Saved startup docking is respected; late-created views can use an already drawn anchor. Only named legacy Schematic/Layout/Setup/Parameter Debugger placements remain.",
    "Manager menu check marks use registered no-argument queries. Public interface version 9 remains C-compatible without STL/SDK/SDL headers. Input order follows the caller; new callbacks find arguments by key.",
    "Modal dialogs defer pending window focus. Removed ToolWindows resource state/drawing, EditorApp resource dialog callbacks and layout state, DefaultObjectConfiguration and the parallel per-type default dock map."
  ],
